<article class="caal-information-panel" lang="en">
  <h2>CAAL Vocabulary Explorer</h2>
  <p>The Central Asian Archaeological Landscapes (CAAL) project works with local partners to document archaeological sites and landscapes across Central Asia. Its multilingual vocabularies support consistent descriptions of sites, cultural periods and related heritage records.</p>
  <h3>Explore the vocabularies</h3>
  <p>Browse the hierarchy or search by term. Concept pages show available labels and definitions, related concepts and links to other vocabularies.</p>
  <h3 id="caal-citing">Citing and reusing terms</h3>
  <p>When referring to a term in a publication or dataset, give the term label, the vocabulary name and the concept URI. The URI is listed under URI and downloads on the concept page. Vocabulary pages also offer RDF downloads where available.</p>
